From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 04:36:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] docs: add a page explaining which open is required

Several feature areas need an open that is not obvious from the namespace layout, and optics
are the worst case: Lens is a plain module under the FSharpPlus namespace, so opening the
parent looks sufficient and is not. lens.fsx already carries an inline comment noting a second
open is needed for length and traverse, which suggests this trips people up.

The new page states which four modules are AutoOpen (Operators, GenericBuilders, Parsing,
Memoization), which are not, and gives a lookup table from what you want to what to open. It
also covers two consequences: the extension modules shadow their FSharp.Core namesakes so open
order can change which function you get, and examples should carry their own opens because
readers copy the snippet rather than the file.

Registered in FSharpPlus.Docs so it is compiled, and linked from index.fsx so it is reachable.
